### Unified PubMed Evidence Context (Same evidence for all experimental conditions)
Title: Impact of ALK rearrangement on survival in resected lung adenocarcinoma: A real-world analysis.
Abstract: The prognostic significance of ALK rearrangement after curative-intent resection of non-small-cell lung cancer (NSCLC) remains uncertain. Although the ALINA trial established adjuvant alectinib for resected ALK-positive NSCLC, patients with contemporary stage IA-IB disease were not fully represented. We evaluated stage-stratified outcomes of ALK-rearranged lung adenocarcinoma within an EGFR-excluded framework.

---

Title: Real-world evolution of first-line ALK-positive NSCLC management in Spain.
Abstract: To describe real-world management of patients with ALK-positive advanced or metastatic NSCLC receiving first-line therapy in Spain, and to assess shifts in treatment patterns following the pricing and reimbursement of lorlatinib for first-line treatment in Spain.

---

Title: Limited Impact of Adjuvant Chemotherapy in ALK-Positive Stage II-III Lung Adenocarcinoma: A Multicenter CReGYT-03 ALK Study.
Abstract: Alectinib was approved in 2024 as an adjuvant therapy for resected ALK-positive non-small-cell lung cancer (NSCLC) based on the ALINA trial. However, the role of cytotoxic adjuvant chemotherapy in this molecular subset remains uncertain. We evaluated the prognostic impact of cytotoxic adjuvant chemotherapy according to ALK status in patients with stage II-III lung adenocarcinoma.

